Amdahl's law states that the maximum speedup of a task using multiple processors is given by the formula: 
\begin{equation} \text{Speedup} = \frac{1}{(1 - P) + \frac{P}{N}} 
\text{where } P \text{ is the proportion of the task that can be parallelized and } N \text{ is the number of processors.} 
